      "annotation" : {
        "createdBy" : [ "Carrine Blank" ],
        "definition" : [ "A mixture of peptones (pancreatic digest of casein and peptic digest of animal/mammalian tissue - meat), used for the culturing of microorganisms." ],
        "definition source" : [ "From BD Bionutrients Technical Manual (3rd edition revised).:\n\nBBL™ Polypeptone™ Peptone is a mixture of peptones made up of equal parts of pancreatic digest of casein and peptic digest of animal tissue. Polypeptone Peptone includes the high content of amino acids and small polypeptides characteristic of pancreatic digest of casein and the larger polypeptides characteristic of peptic digest of animal tissue.\n\nAsh content is 9.7%\nNaCl content is 2.7%" ]
      },
